<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<model version="5.1.3" links="1">
 <documentation>Dining Philosopher Problem (DPP) for RP2040 boards on the Earle Philhower arduino-pico core, using the QP/C++ 7.3.4 QV kernel from qp-arduino. The example demonstrates:

1. Multiple active objects (5 Philosophers and 1 Table AO)
2. Two active object classes (Philo and Table inside the package &quot;AOs&quot;)
3. State machines associated with Philo and Table
4. Publish/subscribe, direct posting and dynamic events from an event pool
5. The concept of a Board Support Package (BSP), kept in bsp.cpp

----
# Board configuration

Built for the qp-arduino RP2040 qualification fixture (mouse-joystick-pcb rev 0) with -DQP_ARDUINO_FIXTURE_MOUSE_JOYSTICK_PCB=1: the &quot;LED&quot; is FW_TRIG0 (GP25) and the tick-ISR probe is FW_TRIG1 (GP21), both visible on the LA5032 through InstrumentPort-40. Without that flag the LED is LED_BUILTIN. QS output goes to the USB CDC port; QSPY/QView attach there. See examples/dpp_bsp-rp2040/README.md.</documentation>
 <!--${qpcpp}-->
 <framework name="qpcpp"/>
